{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5zZhPXgUsDBcHwtrSA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `fetcher` package is now async, and all 6 tests pass (`python -m pytest -q`). I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **`Client`**:\n  - `get`, `get_many` and `close` are all async, and `async with` works.\n  - The transport is an optional async callable, and the default one uses `asyncio.sleep`.\n  - Retries follow the same policy as before: they happen only on `TransientError`, with exponential backoff.\n- **`get_many`**: it runs requests concurrently, capped by `max_concurrency` (default 5). Results keep input order, and per-URL errors come back as `FetchError` in the list.\n- **`aggregate.summarize`**: it is now async and returns the same shape.\n- **`fetcher/sync.py`**: `fetch_all(urls, transport=None)` runs `get_many` under `asyncio.run`. I also exported `sync` from `fetcher/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests**: I ported the three existing tests to plain `asyncio.run`, so no pytest-asyncio dependency is needed. I added three more:\n  - the concurrency cap and result order;\n  - no retry on a non-transient error;\n  - the sync wrapper."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4397,"cache_read_input_tokens":31629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4397},"output_tokens":397,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86afaf90-f01a-4edb-96c9-51ca834c2794","uuid":"e01cd6fe-1078-4524-a510-a6b8a8a93ae4","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:50:39.083Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5zYwzD4SEGu1saSqyH"}
